@larsrc-google Apologies for not working on this. My lack of Java experience made it cumbersome to create a good test case. Do I understand correctly that you do see the problem with interrupts? How do you suggest this PR should proceed, shall I fix your code comments or do you suggest other/bigger changes?

About the InterruptedIoException: I was assuming that the interrupt was caused by resetResponseChecker rather than putRequest which performs IO but I agree that leaving the worker stdin corrupted is a problem. In our case we use the --worker_quit_after_build flag (because of another issue with file locking on Windows) which I think makes this less of an issue though.

Also I'm not really sure I know what you refer to by the new dynamic execution implementation. Is that what is in use right now?
